1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,896
The saved school reading index assigns eleven Week 10 rows. Each guide
below keeps its book, chapters, pages and focus visible, then explains
the main learning ideas in English and Chinese.

2
00:00:13,896 --> 00:00:27,504
This is a bilingual learning aid, not a replacement for the assigned
text. If the exact school edition is unavailable or a candidate page
points to a different topic, the mismatch is stated instead of
silently corrected.

3
00:00:27,504 --> 00:00:59,376
The recovered course copies now identify the actual VSM and CPSC page
contents. VSM includes the visible older-adult documentation task,
while the CPSC literal pages cover oxygen and an attribution page
rather than the named intimate routes. The complete named rectal and
vaginal section is taught separately. The March2025 and June2026 BCPEG
copies agree on these four assigned cards; current service details
remain a separate layer.

4
00:00:59,376 --> 00:01:34,344
All eleven assigned readers now contain source-specific English and
Chinese explanations. The service export includes behavioral transfers
and palliative symptom care beyond the five named codes. The remaining
differences are explicit: the cardiovascular locator is unavailable in
the identified book, some chapter labels do not match literal page
topics, and nursing procedures do not create paramedic authority. Use
the explained literal ranges and separately identified named topics
without pretending their locators are identical.

5
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:46,296
BCPEG is the saved school-exam snapshot for LOC, critical history,
Entonox and methoxyflurane. Its medication language is a reading
target, not a stand-alone order.

6
00:01:46,296 --> 00:02:00,552
Current BCEHS guidance and current legislation govern practice. Verify
the school’s adopted revision with the instructor. A historical page,
nursing procedure or topic label does not create PCP authority.

7
00:02:00,552 --> 00:02:12,816
First open the assigned source and read the surrounding context, not
only the sentence that matches a keyword. Identify what the source
actually claims and which provider or setting it describes.

8
00:02:12,816 --> 00:02:24,792
Then close the text and explain the concept in your own English words.
Restate it in Chinese while preserving the key English clinical term.
Finish with a new application question.

9
00:02:24,792 --> 00:02:38,688
The Week 10 theme connects agitation, refusal and palliative care. A
behavior change can be medical; a refusal can be capable; and a
palliative goal does not remove the need to assess an acute change.

10
00:02:38,688 --> 00:02:50,496
Across all sources, keep three boundaries visible: the patient’s own
goals, the current legal/service pathway, and the limits of the
available edition or assigned pages.

11
00:02:50,496 --> 00:03:23,040
The school names arrhythmia risk in psychiatric crisis. The actual
cardiovascular chapter provides rhythm and electrolyte mechanisms, not
a dedicated psychiatry page at the assigned locator. Connect those
mechanisms to the real patient: distress and exertion can increase
demand, while illness, medicines, substances or fluid losses may add
risk. A psychiatric history does not explain away collapse, abnormal
breathing, poor perfusion or a changing ECG.

12
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:48,864
Obtain the actual exposure timeline and a technically credible
recording when indicated, while continuing immediate support. Do not
diagnose a drug-induced rhythm from a medicine list or assume a normal
first measurement ends the concern. Describe the observed change,
relevant symptoms and uncertainty, reduce avoidable exertion and
request the appropriate help through the current behavioural and
medical pathways.

13
00:03:48,864 --> 00:04:22,752
QT spans ventricular activation and recovery, and QTc applies a
specified rate correction. A prolonged interval can raise concern, but
does not mean that torsades must occur. Torsades is not every
polymorphic ventricular tachycardia, and the school source’s old
mandatory six-hundred-millisecond wording is not a universal
definition. Interpret the preceding rhythm, measurement quality,
symptoms and broader context rather than measuring through a chaotic
tachycardia as if it were a normal beat.

14
00:04:22,752 --> 00:04:54,096
Low potassium or other electrolyte changes, relevant medicines and
concurrent illness can alter risk, but a waveform cannot give a serum
concentration or identify one cause. In an original fainting-and-
distress case, assess breathing and circulation, confirm the recording
and seek appropriate assistance. Do not invent an electrolyte dose. Do
not abruptly stop chronic therapy. Do not select a sedating medicine
merely because a class name appears in the history.
